    "number": 99,
    "title": "docs: reconcile Linux-only performance plan in work guide",
    "body": "Refs #30. Companion to draft #77's Linux-only performance replan.\n\nReplace the early budget row's Windows/WSL comparison with repeated Linux hook profiles, real worker-spawn handoff, bounded descendant cleanup and reviewed budgets. Refresh the paginated backlog inputs and exact primary coverage. Reconcile observed #54 closure without claiming adapter acceptance, and record #59's source merge while #50 remains open. Retain the separately dated history and all nine architecture viewers: the measurement plan does not change the delivered Linux ownership or command path.\n\nNo measurement implementation, benchmark runs, CI edits, installation, devices or public publication are included. #77 stays draft and #30 stays open. Repository-wide Windows policy and CI cleanup remain separate.\n\nValidation: Node 24 npm ci, workflow checks and 13 workflow tests; Python guide build and five maintenance tests; browser checks at widths 320–1440; git diff --check. Inventory: three current specifications, three archives; 106 primary open issues, 12 guides, 48 roadmap nodes and nine unchanged viewers.\n\nThis planning coordinator owns both candidates. Independent replan reviews are recorded below. Guide-source synchronization remains pending reviewed merge; public publication and live verification are outside this request. Do not treat this PR as early-stage performance acceptance.\n\n\n## Replan review receipt\n\nIndependent read-only Standards and Specification reviews found no P0–P3 findings in the planning delta `14c5f733cb48201014abea0e9043b1959e6690c6...31a0c2b1ee4b4c1c9358b2911c9c25f641827f1e` and guide delta `995d784c39e67ab4250ff2890a4789cb4dd9c3fa...588aa436fcad02e9ff6b5a7f8b03d17c616810e2`. Both worktrees were clean; each merge-base equaled its recorded base. This review does not approve the original measurement implementation or satisfy Linux performance acceptance.\n\nPlanning validation passed on Node 24: three current specifications, one active change, three archives and ten workflow tests. Guide validation passed: three current specifications, three archives, thirteen workflow tests, five maintenance tests and browser checks at widths 320–1440. All nine architecture viewers are unchanged. Hosted checks and any applicable candidate approval remain separate merge gates. No merge or public publication is included in this planning delivery.\n",
