    "number": 77,
    "title": "perf: prepare Linux hook baseline; evidence and budgets pending",
    "body": "Refs #30. Draft preparation for the early Linux baseline/budget stage. This does not release Hub #3 or complete overall #30.\n\nThe September 10 replan replaces native Windows/WSL comparison and executable-forwarding measurements with the real Linux hook from delivered [Nanoleaf PR #57](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/57), merge `2558df5a2fc543247b0c75898ef0260ba3ea264b`. Windows interop availability is no longer the blocker.\n\nRemaining work is to pin the executed Linux source set, prove isolated state and bounded cleanup of detached children, and measure the actual hook from process launch through return. Include parsing, admission/commit and real Linux worker-spawn handoff; keep background readiness/cleanup, burst makespan and component timings distinct. Repeat comparable 1/10/50 synthetic-session profiles, exercise isolated failure cases, and freeze reviewed numeric performance budgets. No-op launch timing cannot complete full-hook coverage.\n\nExisting legacy admission and released-validator tools, pins and raw receipts are unchanged. Nine admission profiles, six validator profiles, fourteen focused tests and external consumer regressions are historical preparation evidence, not full Linux hook results. Preparation reviews and 24 successful push/PR jobs at `14c5f733cb48201014abea0e9043b1959e6690c6` do not approve this revised candidate.\n\nThis update changes proposal, design, specification, tasks, performance documentation and the guide maintenance record only. Node 24 setup, workflow validation and ten workflow tests pass: three current specifications, one active change and three archives. The active `gh-30-shared-monitor-performance` change remains unfinished and unarchived. Task 1.3 now reflects the previously recorded CI integration; new Linux implementation/evidence tasks remain unchecked.\n\n[Guide companion #99](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/pull/99) updates current-main guide inputs/output so this old branch does not replace the delivered Linux diagrams. This planning coordinator owns both candidates. Guide-source synchronization remains pending the companion's reviewed merge. Public publication and live verification are outside this request.\n\nRepository-wide Windows CI removal and cost reduction are separate work. Current CI, lifecycle/provider policy, older planning context, portability code and legacy source branches retain Windows elements; historical receipts also retain their original provenance. These are flagged for the user, not accepted as new Windows performance prerequisites. Existing configured CI gates remain until separately replaced.\n\nNo new measurement implementation, benchmark run, CI edit, installation, personal hook/settings change, client session or device operation is included. Nanoleaf #55 retains installed and physical acceptance. Independent replan reviews are recorded below; final delivery reviews and current-head CI remain required after implementation.\n\n\n## Replan review receipt\n\nIndependent read-only Standards and Specification reviews found no P0–P3 findings in the planning delta `14c5f733cb48201014abea0e9043b1959e6690c6...31a0c2b1ee4b4c1c9358b2911c9c25f641827f1e` and guide delta `995d784c39e67ab4250ff2890a4789cb4dd9c3fa...588aa436fcad02e9ff6b5a7f8b03d17c616810e2`. Both worktrees were clean; each merge-base equaled its recorded base. This review does not approve the original measurement implementation or satisfy Linux performance acceptance.\n\nPlanning validation passed on Node 24: three current specifications, one active change, three archives and ten workflow tests. Guide validation passed: three current specifications, three archives, thirteen workflow tests, five maintenance tests and browser checks at widths 320–1440. All nine architecture viewers are unchanged. Hosted checks and any applicable candidate approval remain separate merge gates. No merge or public publication is included in this planning delivery.\n",
